    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who commands the highest efficiency score at 82.13. His leadoff spot against Gusto provides a premium opportunity for stolen base production, a critical need given our aggressive 5x5 strategy; the 14% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage and the 10% boost from batting at the top of the order make him an indispensable anchor. Similarly, **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30) and **Josh Smith** (64.66) are prime candidates for high-output nights, as both benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Gibson, whose 5.35 xERA is the most exploitable figure on today\u2019s board. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a core tactical play at 73.11, as his elite 0.442 xwOBA offsets the slight park-factor penalty, ensuring we maintain a high floor for HR and RBI production regardless of the matchup against Kirby.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the final utility spot, where **Carson Benge** (51.63) narrowly missed the cut behind the stability of our active infielders. While **Carson Benge** benefits from the favorable SP skill profile of Bradford, his L/L platoon disadvantage creates enough variance to favor the higher baseline efficiency of **Chase Meidroth** (52.52). We are closely monitoring the status of **Trea Turner** (49.88); while his score remains elevated by his #2 spot in the order, he faces a daunting matchup against Henderson. Despite the elite speed he provides, his efficiency is currently suppressed by Henderson\u2019s ability to hold runners and a tough 2.97 xERA. We will monitor the real-time game flow closely, though with **Colt Keith** still sidelined on the IL and **Hector Rodriguez** out of the lineup, our depth is thinner than usual, necessitating a disciplined approach to our remaining game caps.",
